{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And humble</b> — it has no parallel form [in the root], like <i>ramus</i>. The meaning: if you have strength, humble the proud. He mentioned two of the proud: one, Behemoth, which is on land; and the second, Leviathan, which is in the sea."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:25.931513877Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}